  "conditions": [
    "The Rust default MIT/Apache2 alternative applies only where the original root declaration and per-file notices permit it. Preserve root COPYRIGHT and all individually scoped LLVM Apache2/LLVM exception, legacy LLVM NCSA, Tachyon BSD and Unicode grants. No source-wide relicense or exception expansion is asserted.",
    "Retain the complete original source archive and complete original copyright aggregate bound by this record, including all per-file author attribution, original font/OFL notices and source Cargo declarations. Embedded SPDX license-text catalog entries are reference data, not declarations that Rust is licensed under every example license in that catalog.",
    "All original vendored package alternatives remain as declared in their own Cargo manifests and files. Root manifests cover 1511 vendor entries. Three entries using only license-file are resolved by the actual ring, encoding_rs and Fuchsia original licenses; no license is inferred from their filenames alone.",
    "Keep ring ISC/Google and fiat MIT attribution plus original OpenSSL/SSLeay acknowledgements, Eric Young cryptographic credit and Tim Hudson credit. Do not rename covered products OpenSSL or relicense covered OpenSSL/SSLeay code under GPL. These tool-source scopes do not assert their presence in the installed Rust standard library.",
    "Keep separate GPL3 gccjit and CDDL1 Inferno source-tool terms and corresponding sources. Do not treat those optional source tools as components linked into the installed standard library or combine their licenses into an assertion of GPL/CDDL linkage compatibility. CDDL files remain under CDDL, modifications carry contributor identification, and no extra source restrictions are imposed.",
    "Keep original encoding_rs Mozilla attribution, MIT/Apache alternative, WHATWG BSD3 data credits/nonendorsement and expressly designated PD/CC0 test scopes. Unmodified original font files retain their original font names, authors and individual licenses. All source/notice collection, reconstruction and actual runtime linkage are independent final release checks."
  ],
  "review_limits": "Original root COPYRIGHT reading is inherited. Original source manifests retain their independent declaration scopes. This does not claim fresh manual reading of every repeated license text or any binary reconstruction result.",
